# CLAUDE.md

This repository is the Coordinator of {{ fleet_name }}, a Fleet of Mechs.
It holds no records. Each member is its own repository, with its own
`CLAUDE.md`; inside a member, that file governs.

## What lives here

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `fleet.yaml` | The one list of members and the relationships between them. Every command reads it |
| `src/{{ fleet_slug }}_coordinator/schema/fleet_schema.yaml` | The Fleet model `fleet.yaml` follows |
| `canon/` | The files every member carries byte for byte, and `manifest.yaml` with their sha256 |
| `src/{{ fleet_slug }}_coordinator/` | The `fleet` command (`uv run fleet --help`) |
| `cache/members/` | Read-only clones of the members, from `just fetch`. Not committed |

## Rules

- `fleet.yaml` is the source of truth for what a member is and how its
  records link to other members'. A member's own Copier answers follow it:
  `just answers <member>` prints them. Never change a member's
  `fleet_links` by hand.
- A relationship is declared before any record uses it. Links outside a
  declared relationship fail `just audit`.
- A shared ontology term between two records is a lead for a link, not a
  link. A link states a relation, how it was established (its basis), and
  the target's commit that was checked.
- Canon files change here, and only here. Then `just canon-refresh`, merge,
  and sync every member (`change-canon`). Never edit a canon file in a member.
- Nothing here pushes to a member. Changes reach a member by a pull request
  in that member, made from its own checkout.
- `just qc` must pass before a commit here. `just audit` is the Fleet's
  check, and needs `just fetch` first.
- Agents that read text anyone can write (member records, issues) get no
  write permission. The audit workflow runs no agent; a plain step opens
  its issue.

## Skills

Skills are in `.claude/skills/`.

| Skill | Use it to |
|---|---|
| `onboard-mech` | add a Mech to the Fleet, new or existing |
| `add-relationship` | declare how one member's records link to another's, and carry it into the subject member |
| `change-canon` | change a shared file and release it to every member |

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `just qc` | Lint, `fleet.yaml`, the canon, tests, docs build |
| `just fetch [member...]` | Clone or refresh members under `cache/members/` |
| `just audit [--root id=PATH]` | Every member: answers agree, one canon pin, links resolve |
| `just check-links` | Only the links |
| `just status` | One row per member |
| `just answers <member>` | The member's Copier answers |
| `just sync <member> <path> [--apply]` | The canon into a member's checkout |
| `just canon-refresh` | Rewrite the manifest's sha256s after a canon change |

`--root id=PATH` points a command at a local checkout of a member instead of
its clone, for work not yet pushed.
